# Alert reliability and accuracy

When an alert is wrong, flapping, or pages on a healthy state, fix the
expr. Do not silence, widen `for` as a substitute for a better query, or
delete the signal.

- Page on **user-visible or operator-actionable** failure. Gate on the
  symptom (waiting clients, 5xx, probe fail), not a gauge that sits full
  on purpose.
- Prefer `avg_over_time` / `rate` / `increase` over a raw instantaneous
  gauge when the series is bursty. Pair a ratio with an absolute rate
  when volume can hide errors.
- Thresholds must match live values, not a round number. Exclude hosts
  that are meant to be out (see existing `host!~` / `instance!~` patterns).
- Critical vs warning: outage or data loss is critical; headroom and
  saturation are warning. Match neighbouring rules in
  `services/mimir-rules.nix`.
- After a change, restart `mimir.service` on both obs nodes
  (`restartIfChanged = false`; `deploy.mdc`).
